TPUs through this interface.

00:27:20.350 --> 00:27:22.960
When we talk about training,
what does that really mean?

00:27:22.960 --> 00:27:26.640
What we're doing is we have
a cloudml_train function.

00:27:26.640 --> 00:27:28.890
That's really taking
all the R code,

00:27:28.890 --> 00:27:31.500
uploading it into our
cluster of servers,

00:27:31.500 --> 00:27:35.640
installing all the dependencies,
and now using the cloud

00:27:35.640 --> 00:27:37.880
for massive scale there.

00:27:37.880 --> 00:27:40.380
Andrie also talked about
TF Runs to really create

00:27:40.380 --> 00:27:42.870
a systematic approach
around experimenting.

00:27:42.870 --> 00:27:44.880
And really that
concept around champion

00:27:44.880 --> 00:27:47.880
versus challenger models,
and keep track of all those.

00:27:47.880 --> 00:27:51.220
And that's traditionally
using grid search techniques.

00:27:51.220 --> 00:27:53.880
Another value of Cloud
ML Engine is we actually

00:27:53.880 --> 00:27:57.660
have hyperparameter tuning
using Bayesian optimization that

00:27:57.660 --> 00:28:00.240
does it automatically for
you with an input file

00:28:00.240 --> 00:28:02.790
where you give it some
guidelines on what evaluation

00:28:02.790 --> 00:28:06.064
