00:28:19.980 --> 00:28:23.030
The one great thing
about TensorFlow models,

00:28:23.030 --> 00:28:25.410
also they are language
and platform agnostic.

00:28:25.410 --> 00:28:27.510
They're binary files
that can be consumed

00:28:27.510 --> 00:28:31.450
by any type of libraries and
converted into REST APIs.

00:28:31.450 --> 00:28:33.840
So in this case, we're
going to use the Deploy

00:28:33.840 --> 00:28:37.680
function to really publish
or register this model

00:28:37.680 --> 00:28:39.579
into a cloud registry.

00:28:39.579 --> 00:28:41.370
And now a number of
developers and analysts

00:28:41.370 --> 00:28:44.400
can now consume it
as a REST API call,

00:28:44.400 --> 00:28:45.939
whether that be through R--

00:28:45.939 --> 00:28:47.730
in this case, we use
the Predict function--

00:28:47.730 --> 00:28:51.060
but it could be a Python
developer, a Java application,

00:28:51.060 --> 00:28:54.240
a mobile application that
all consume the same model

00:28:54.240 --> 00:28:57.060
with the appropriate
input provided

00:28:57.060 --> 00:29:01.080
and the response provided
in the appropriate format.

